  Journal                  = {Geophysical Research Letters},
  Year                     = {2002},
  Number                   = {8},
  Pages                    = {23--1--23--4},
  Volume                   = {29},

  Abstract                 = {We examine the consequences of using four exchange coefficient versus wind speed parameterisations on the air-sea {COextsubscript{2}} flux estimation, using one year of satellite wind speed measurements at global scale. Estimates of the global net {COextsubscript{2}} flux to the ocean vary from 1.2 to 2.7 GtC yr$-$1. Additionnaly, we show 1) that the relative importance of outgassing and absorption fluxes is dependent on the form of the relationships due to a correlation between the direction of the flux and wind speed and 2) that differences on global net air-sea flux deduced from different K parameterisations are primarily due to parameterisation differences in the wind speed range between 4 and 17 ms$-$1.},
