  month       = MAR,
  number      = {3},
  pages       = {744-748},
  volume      = {52},
  abstract    = {Resonances of solitons in one-dimensional space are studied
theoretically taking the Sawada-Kotera equation with a nonvanishing
boundary condition as an example. Two solitons near the resonant state
exhibit the new phenomena. They interact with each other through
emitting and absorbing third soliton. They are transmuted into
singular solitons after colliding with each other. Two solitons at the
resonant state fuse after colliding with each other, or a soliton
splits into two solitons.},
